### Step 8 — Moderation. VS Code "REST Client".
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080

### 1. A normal user
# @name user
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "identifier": "chef_kabir", "password": "Cookify2026!" }

### 2. Abusive comment → 400 CONTENT_BLOCKED "warning 1 of 3" (warning email in console)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/recipes/1/comments
Authorization: Bearer {{user.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "body": "this is sh1t" }

### 3. Admin login (demo admin)
# @name admin
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "identifier": "admin", "password": "Cookify2026!" }

### 4. Users with warnings
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/users?status=WARNED
Authorization: Bearer {{admin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 5. A user's warnings (replace 7 with the user's id from request 4)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/users/7/warnings
Authorization: Bearer {{admin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 6. Ban for 7 days (or { "permanent": true, ... }) — removes their content
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/users/7/ban
Authorization: Bearer {{admin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "days": 7, "reason": "Abusive comments" }

### 7. Unban (also resets warnings)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/users/7/unban
Authorization: Bearer {{admin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 8. Non-admin → 403
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/users
Authorization: Bearer {{user.response.body.accessToken}}
